Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?Fix=20#51:=20Chat=20title=20is=20cut=20off?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20with=20"=E2=80=A6"=20even=20though=20it=20fits?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chat title is built by `titleFrom` in `src/lib/chat/store.ts:48-53`.
It is off by one. The check is `flat.length < TITLE_LENGTH`
(TITLE_LENGTH = 42), so a question that is exactly 42 characters after
whitespace is flattened fails the check. It gets cut to its first 41
characters plus "…". The result is still 42 characters long, so it would
have fit as it was. The title ends in "…" with only its last character
swapped out, which makes it look as if nothing is missing. Longer
questions are cut as intended. The sidebar's CSS `truncate`
(`src/components/chat-sidebar.tsx:88`) only adds its own ellipsis when
the text overflows, so it is not the cause. The existing test
(`src/lib/chat/chat.test.ts:100-106`) only covers 100 characters and
very short input, never the 42-character boundary.
---
 src/lib/chat/store.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/chat/store.ts b/src/lib/chat/store.ts
index 8a1f17c4..501daaf4 100644
--- a/src/lib/chat/store.ts
+++ b/src/lib/chat/store.ts
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ const TITLE_LENGTH = 42;
 
 export function titleFrom(text: string): string {
   const flat = text.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim();
-  return flat.length < TITLE_LENGTH ? flat : `${flat.slice(0, TITLE_LENGTH - 1)}…`;
+  return flat.length <= TITLE_LENGTH ? flat : `${flat.slice(0, TITLE_LENGTH - 1)}…`;
 }
 
